UPDATE scholarships SET title = $$Axel Adler Scholarship (University of Gothenburg)$$, provider = $$University of Gothenburg$$, country = $$Sweden$$, coverage_type = $$Tuition Waiver$$, amount_usd_value = 0, award_amount = NULL, award_currency = $$SEK$$, award_period = $$year$$, award_basis = $$variable$$, deadline = $$Two stages for the 2027 round: (1) apply for the programme at universityadmissions.se with a University of Gothenburg programme as your first priority by 15 January 2027, and pay the application fee and document your eligibility by 1 February 2027; (2) the scholarship application itself is by invitation only - eligible applicants receive an email around 10 February 2027 and must submit between 10 February and 8 March 2027. Results by email on 12 April 2027 (master's) and 15 April 2027 (bachelor's). deadline_date stores the real scholarship-application close (8 March 2027), not the admission deadline.$$ , deadline_date = $$2027-03-08$$, deadline_type = $$fixed$$, opening_date = NULL, deadline_range_start = NULL, deadline_range_end = NULL, rounds = $$[{"name": "Axel Adler Scholarship 2027", "status": "programme application (GU first priority) by 2027-01-15; application fee and eligibility documents by 2027-02-01; invitation email around 2027-02-10; scholarship application 2027-02-10 to 2027-03-08; results 2027-04-12 (master applicants) / 2027-04-15 (bachelor applicants)", "deadline_date": "2027-03-08"}, {"name": "Annual pattern", "status": "each autumn-intake cycle repeats this shape: first admission round closing mid-January, invitation-only scholarship window in February-early March, results in April", "deadline_date": null}]$$, recurrence = $$annual$$, expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, degree_levels = $$["Bachelor's", "Master's"]$$, eligible_majors = $$["All Majors"]$$, eligible_countries = $$["All - no citizenship restriction; the condition is being required to pay tuition fees in Sweden"]$$, min_gpa = NULL, min_ielts = NULL, financial_need_based = false, merit_based = true, description = $$The University of Gothenburg's main scholarship for fee-paying students (official Axel Adler page, last modified 8 October 2026, and the university's "Requirements for the Axel Adler Scholarship 2027" PDF - both fetched 2026-10-28). It is a full tuition-fee waiver for the whole programme (four semesters/120 credits for master's, two semesters for 1-year master's, six semesters/180 credits for bachelor's), funded by the Adlerbertska Scholarship Foundation, the Adlerbertska Grant Foundation and the Swedish Council for Higher Education (UHR), with the foundations paying the fee directly to the university - plus FAS+ insurance cover (Kammarkollegiet) for scholarship holders. It does NOT cover living or accommodation expenses or travel. The feature that makes it unusually accessible: there is no citizenship restriction - any applicant who is required to pay tuition fees in Sweden can be eligible, Uzbekistan included. Allocation is per programme: one scholarship for each master's programme and each eligible bachelor's programme (eligible bachelor's: Software Engineering and Management, Computer Science and AI, International Relations, Business and Economics, and three BFA craft programmes), four in total across the Artistic Faculty, and up to ten additional awards if funds allow - so your odds depend on the programme you pick. The mechanics are strict: the Gothenburg programme must be your first priority at universityadmissions.se (if you apply to several GU programmes, only the first-priority one can carry the scholarship); studies application by 15 January 2027; fee and eligibility documents by 1 February 2027; the scholarship application is then by invitation (email around 10 February 2027), submitted 10 February-8 March 2027, consisting of a CV and a letter of motivation written in the application system (max 3,000 characters each, no uploads); academic staff rank on those two texts plus academic merits; results 12 April 2027 (master's) / 15 April 2027 (bachelor's). Holding it requires completing at least 75% of each semester's credits and having your residence permit in time to start (no permit on time = withdrawn, and permit delay is not a valid deferment reason). It cannot be combined with another tuition-covering scholarship. Sibling schemes have their own records: the Axel Adler Scholarship for Sustainability (record 967; same application, for sustainability-focused master's) and the Richard C. Malmsten Memorial Foundation Scholarship for Graduate School business master's (record 988).$$ , requirements = $$From the fetched Axel Adler Scholarship 2027 requirements (University of Gothenburg International Centre PDF) and the scholarship page. Eligibility: be required to pay tuition fees in Sweden (no citizenship restriction; you need not have paid the tuition fee before applying); apply in the international admission round for an international campus-based programme at the University of Gothenburg ranked as your first priority, submitting the studies application by 15 January 2027 and paying the application fee and documenting eligibility via universityadmissions.se by 1 February 2027. Eligible students are then invited by email (around 10 February 2027) and must submit the scholarship application between 10 February and 8 March 2027 - late applications are not considered. The whole assessed content is a CV and letter of motivation written in the scholarship system (max 3,000 characters each; documents cannot be uploaded), ranked by academic staff with academic merits also considered. To be awarded you must be admitted to a full-time master's programme or one of the seven listed full-time bachelor's programmes; online programmes are excluded. Conditions: the waiver covers the tuition fee for the whole programme and FAS+ insurance, never living/accommodation costs (show separate funds, also for the residence permit); it cannot be combined with another tuition-covering scholarship (you may apply for several but hold only one); keep at least 75% of each semester's credits with regular follow-ups; obtain the residence permit in time to start or the scholarship is withdrawn; notify the university if your fee status changes; suspension for disciplinary reasons may end it. No minimum GPA and no scholarship-level English score are published (programme entry requirements apply), so none are encoded here - the earlier stored 3.3 GPA / 6.5 IELTS figures were importer leftovers and have been removed.$$ , website_url = $$https://www.gu.se/en/study-in-gothenburg/apply/scholarships-for-fee-paying-students/axel-adler-scholarship$$, source_url = $$https://www.gu.se/en/study-in-gothenburg/apply/scholarships-for-fee-paying-students/axel-adler-scholarship$$, application_url = $$https://www.gu.se/en/study-in-gothenburg/apply/scholarships-for-fee-paying-students/axel-adler-scholarship$$, funding_type = $$Full tuition fee waiver for the whole programme, paid by the funding foundations directly to the university, plus FAS+ insurance$$, tuition_coverage = $$100% of the programme tuition fee for its full length (120 credits master's / 60 credits 1-year master's / 180 credits bachelor's); living expenses, accommodation and travel are explicitly not covered.$$ , living_allowance = NULL, travel_allowance = NULL, accommodation = NULL, application_fee = NULL, english_requirements = $$No scholarship-level English score is published; the English requirement of the chosen programme's admission applies.$$ , required_documents = $$["Programme application at universityadmissions.se with a University of Gothenburg campus-based programme as first priority (by 15 January 2027), application fee paid and eligibility documented by 1 February 2027", "CV written in the scholarship application system (max 3,000 characters; no uploads/attachments possible)", "Letter of motivation written in the scholarship application system (max 3,000 characters) highlighting qualifications from the CV", "Separate proof of funds for living costs (needed for the residence permit; the scholarship covers tuition only)"]$$, application_status = $$upcoming$$, verification_status = $$verified$$, source_reliability = 10, is_active = true, university_id = 136, notes = $$BATCH 27 UPLIFT rel 9 -> 10 (2026-10-28): GU Axel Adler page (last modified 2026-10-08) and the official 'Requirements for the Axel Adler Scholarship 2027' PDF both fetched first-hand today, supplying the genuine 2027 scholarship window (invitation ~10 Feb 2027; apply 10 Feb-8 Mar 2027) now encoded as deadline_date 2027-03-08/'fixed' with status 'upcoming' - replacing deadline_type 'annual', no-date, status 'open'. Importer minima min_gpa 3.3 / min_ielts 6.5 removed (nothing of the kind on fetched pages; the row's own english_requirements already contradicted them). Added from fetch: FAS+ insurance, whole-programme coverage by credits, first-priority-only rule, CV/LoM 3,000-character format, results 12/15 Apr 2027, 75%-credits retention, residence-permit conditions, eligible bachelor list. Malmsten paragraph extracted to its own new record 988; sustainability sibling is 967. Sources: new PDF source 3129 + existing page source 2533 both linked (record previously had no source link). us 130 resynced (availability 'Yes'->'available'; valued_aspect importer artefact 'Swedish C1' replaced). Earlier verification 2026-10-25 (rel 9) had read the scholarship page, business-school page, news page and tuition page.$$ , last_verified_at = now(), last_updated_at = now() WHERE id = 739 RETURNING id, source_reliability;

-- 3) Chalmers 421: re-check only (page still not updated for 2027 -> rel stays 9)
UPDATE scholarships SET notes = notes || $$ RE-CHECKED 2026-10-28 (Batch 27): the official page still states it is 'not yet updated with the information regarding Chalmers scholarships offered in 2027 admission round', so reliability stays 9 until Chalmers publishes the 2027 scheme details; re-fetch confirmed the stored operational claims unchanged (separate portal application after the universityadmissions.se application; window late November 2026 to mid-January 2027 aligning with the programme deadline, not the documentation deadline; prospective students only; financial status disregarded). Revisit for rel 10 once the page updates (expected around the late-November portal opening).$$ , last_verified_at = now(), last_updated_at = now() WHERE id = 421 RETURNING id, source_reliability;

-- 4) New record 988 (Malmsten; previously a paragraph inside 739)
INSERT INTO scholarships (id, title, provider, country, coverage_type, amount_usd_value, deadline, degree_levels, eligible_majors, min_gpa, min_ielts, financial_need_based, merit_based, description, requirements, website_url, eligible_countries, funding_type, tuition_coverage, living_allowance, travel_allowance, accommodation, application_fee, english_requirements, required_documents, application_url, opening_date, deadline_date, deadline_type, deadline_range_start, deadline_range_end, rounds, recurrence, expected_opening_period, expected_deadline_period, application_status, last_verified_at, last_updated_at, verification_status, source_reliability, source_url, notes, is_active, university_id, award_amount, award_currency, award_period, award_basis) VALUES (988, $$Richard C. Malmsten Memorial Foundation Scholarship$$, $$University of Gothenburg - Graduate School, School of Business, Economics and Law$$, $$Sweden$$, $$Partial Tuition$$, 0, $$Awarded once a year. The 2026 application round ran 3 February-17 March 2026 and is closed; information on the 2027 application will be published in November 2026 on the official page linked here - no fixed 2027 deadline is published yet, so none is encoded.$$ , $$["Master's"]$$, $$["Nine Graduate School MSc programmes at the School of Business, Economics and Law: Accounting and Financial Management; Economics; Finance; International Business and Trade; Innovation and Industrial Management; Knowledge Based Entrepreneurship; Logistics and Transport Management; Management; Marketing and Consumption"]$$, NULL, NULL, false, true, $$Aimed squarely at fee-paying applicants to the University of Gothenburg's Graduate School master's programmes at the School of Business, Economics and Law (fetched official page, last modified 15 October 2026). The Richard C. Malmsten Memorial Foundation Scholarship covers part of the tuition fee: SEK 100,000 over two years, applied as a tuition-fee waiver of SEK 25,000 per semester, and it is awarded once a year. It is, in effect, a GMAT competition: applicants admitted to one of the nine listed MSc programmes (Accounting and Financial Management; Economics; Finance; International Business and Trade; Innovation and Industrial Management; Knowledge Based Entrepreneurship; Logistics and Transport Management; Management; Marketing and Consumption) are ranked by their GMAT score, which must be sent to the School directly by the test organisation - and the page is blunt that students without a GMAT score will not be considered. Applicants who put a Graduate School master's as their first priority are prioritised. Two exclusions matter: anyone offered a Swedish Institute scholarship or one of the University of Gothenburg's own study scholarships (such as the Axel Adler Scholarship, record 739) does not qualify for the Malmsten award, so treat it as the fallback layer, not a stackable top-up. Selection is by the School's selection committee and cannot be appealed. It is administered by the Graduate School (contact study.info@gs.gu.se). Timing: the 2026 round was open 3 February-17 March 2026; the next round (for autumn 2027 entry) will be announced on the official page in November 2026.$$ , $$From the fetched official page. Eligibility: (1) you are required to pay tuition fees for education in Sweden; (2) you have applied for one of the School of Business, Economics and Law's nine listed Graduate School MSc programmes. Selection: applicants admitted to one of those programmes are ranked by GMAT score (the score must be sent to the School by the test organisation; the page links the Graduate School's GMAT information for the minimum-score context); applicants without a GMAT score are not considered; first-priority applicants to Graduate School programmes are prioritised. Exclusions: students offered a Swedish Institute scholarship or a University of Gothenburg study scholarship do not qualify. The award covers SEK 100,000 of tuition over two years (SEK 25,000 per semester waiver) - the rest of the tuition fee and all living costs remain the student's. The selection committee's decision is final (not open to appeal). No minimum GPA or scholarship-level English figure is published on the page, so none are encoded; programme admission requirements (including English) apply separately.$$ , $$https://www.gu.se/en/study-in-gothenburg/apply/scholarships-for-fee-paying-students/scholarships-for-students-at-the-school-of-business-economics-and-law$$, $$["Students required to pay tuition fees in Sweden (no country list published)"]$$, $$Tuition fee waiver of SEK 25,000 per semester (SEK 100,000 over two years)$$, $$Part of the tuition fee only: SEK 100,000 across the two-year master's as a SEK 25,000-per-semester waiver; the remaining tuition and all living costs are the student's.$$ , NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $$No scholarship-level English figure is published; the English requirement of the chosen MSc programme's admission applies. A GMAT score is essential for this scholarship's ranking.$$ , $$["Application and admission to one of the nine listed Graduate School MSc programmes (first-priority applicants are prioritised)", "GMAT score sent to the School of Business, Economics and Law directly by the test organisation - no GMAT score, no consideration", "Scholarship application during the announced round window (2026 round: 3 February-17 March 2026; 2027 round to be announced in November 2026)"]$$, $$https://www.gu.se/en/study-in-gothenburg/apply/scholarships-for-fee-paying-students/scholarships-for-students-at-the-school-of-business-economics-and-law$$, NULL, NULL, $$not_published$$, NULL, NULL, $$[{"name": "2026 round", "status": "closed - application was open 3 February to 17 March 2026", "deadline_date": null}, {"name": "Richard C Malmsten Scholarship 2027", "status": "information regarding the 2027 scholarship application will be published in November 2026 on the official page", "deadline_date": null}, {"name": "Annual pattern", "status": "awarded once a year; round window announced on the official page each cycle", "deadline_date": null}]$$, $$annual$$, NULL, NULL, $$upcoming$$, now(), now(), $$verified$$, 10, $$https://www.gu.se/en/study-in-gothenburg/apply/scholarships-for-fee-paying-students/scholarships-for-students-at-the-school-of-business-economics-and-law$$, $$BATCH 27 NEW RECORD (2026-10-28): the Malmsten scheme previously existed only as a paragraph inside the Axel Adler record 739; extracted into its own record after a first-hand fetch of the official GU business-school scholarships page (last modified 2026-10-15; new source 3130). Amount encoded (SEK 100,000, 'total', 'fixed') because the page publishes a single flat figure (SEK 25,000/semester over two years); amount_usd_value 0 per non-USD rule. 2027 round dates are NOT yet published (announcement due November 2026) -> deadline NULL/'not_published' + rounds, status 'upcoming'. The page links a separate GMAT page for minimum-score context; that page was not fetched, so no GMAT number is encoded - only the fetched 'ranked by GMAT; no GMAT, no consideration' rule. university_id 136 (Gothenburg catalogue row); new us 711.$$ , true, 136, 100000, $$SEK$$, $$total$$, $$fixed$$) RETURNING id, title;

-- 5) New record 989 (first Linköping record in the catalogue)
INSERT INTO scholarships (id, title, provider, country, coverage_type, amount_usd_value, deadline, degree_levels, eligible_majors, min_gpa, min_ielts, financial_need_based, merit_based, description, requirements, website_url, eligible_countries, funding_type, tuition_coverage, living_allowance, travel_allowance, accommodation, application_fee, english_requirements, required_documents, application_url, opening_date, deadline_date, deadline_type, deadline_range_start, deadline_range_end, rounds, recurrence, expected_opening_period, expected_deadline_period, application_status, last_verified_at, last_updated_at, verification_status, source_reliability, source_url, notes, is_active, university_id, award_amount, award_currency, award_period, award_basis) VALUES (989, $$LiU International Scholarship$$, $$Linköping University$$, $$Sweden$$, $$Partial Tuition$$, 0, $$The scholarship application opens on the day of the First Notification of Selection Results (master's results: 1 April 2027 for the 2027 round) and stays open only for a short window; exact dates are published on the official LiU scholarships page later (the university's own dates table lists the 2027 scholarship application period as TBD), so no fixed deadline is encoded. The admission deadlines behind it: programme application by 15 January 2027, documents and application fee by 1 February 2027.$$ , $$["Master's"]$$, $$["All Majors"]$$, 3.5, NULL, false, true, $$Linköping University's (LiU) scholarship for outstanding new international master's students who are required to pay tuition fees (fetched official scholarships page, 2026-10-28). The tuition fee of an awarded student is normally reduced by 50% - read that carefully: the university reserves the right to determine each year how many scholarships are offered, what percentage is offered, and the merit process, and its rules speak of the scholarship covering the total tuition fee or part of it, so 50% is the normal case, not a promise (the older '25/50/75%' figures circulating on aggregator sites are not what the current official page says). Since 2026 there is a hard academic floor: only applicants with a GPA of 3.5 or higher on a 4.0 scale, a first or high second class degree, or an equivalent average are considered (the page gives typical equivalents: 75% or above in India, 80-85% or above in China, 8.0/10 or above on 10-point scales), institutional rankings form part of the evaluation, and applications below the minimum standard are not considered at all. The process is back-loaded compared with most Swedish universities: you must have applied in the first admission round on time (application by 15 January, documents by their deadline), ranked a LiU master's programme as priority 1 of 4, and been admitted to that first choice in the First Notification of Selection Results (1 April 2027 for master's in this round); the scholarship application then opens for a short window at that point, eligible students are invited, and no additional documents are needed for the scholarship application itself. Keeping it is conditional: pass at least 75% of first-year courses as registered by 1 July (45 of 60 credits) to receive it for year two; it is rescinded if you later win a Swedish Institute scholarship, if your fee status changes, or if your residence permit is not in place in time for studies. Swedish Institute scholarships usable at LiU are a separate channel (see record 922).$$ , $$From the fetched LiU scholarships page. Minimum academic standard (new criteria from 2026): GPA 3.5 or higher on a 4.0 scale, a first or high second class degree, or an equivalent average (page examples: 75%+ India, 80-85%+ China, 8.0/10+ on 10-point CGPA scales); institutional rankings are considered in the evaluation; applications not meeting the minimum are not considered. You are eligible to apply if ALL of the following hold: you applied by the deadline for the first admission round; you submitted all required documents by the deadline; you chose a master's programme at Linköping University as your first priority (ranked number 1 of 4); you have been admitted to your first choice in the First Notification of Selection Results (master's: 1 April 2027); and you are a citizen of a country outside the EU/EEA/Switzerland who is required to pay tuition fees. The scholarship application period opens on the results day for a short window (2027: early April; exact dates to be published on the page); eligible students are invited to apply before it closes; no additional documents are needed for the scholarship application. Rules once awarded: the offer is valid only for the stated year and programme; it covers the total tuition fee or part of it (normally a 50% reduction) for a workload of 30 credits per semester within the programme (extra courses cost extra), and any remainder of the fee must be paid by the payment deadline; you must pass at least 75% of first-year courses as registered by 1 July (e.g. 45 of 60 credits) to keep it for year two; the scholarship is rescinded if you are awarded a Swedish Institute scholarship, if you cease to be a fee-payer (you must inform LiU in writing), or if you do not obtain a residence permit in time; LiU may revoke it, including for suspended students. No scholarship-level English figure is published - programme admission requirements apply.$$ , $$https://liu.se/en/article/scholarships$$, $$["Citizens of countries outside the EU/EEA/Switzerland who are required to pay tuition fees in Sweden (no country list)"]$$, $$Tuition-fee reduction for new fee-paying master's students - normally 50% (the university sets the percentage and the number of awards each year)$$, $$Normally 50% of the tuition fee (rules allow total or part coverage; the percentage is decided yearly); covers a 30-credits-per-semester workload in the named programme; any remaining fee must be paid by the payment deadline; no living-cost support.$$ , NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $$No scholarship-level English score is published on the fetched page; each master's programme's admission English requirement applies.$$ , $$["First-round master's application at universityadmissions.se submitted on time (2027 round: by 15 January 2027) with a LiU programme ranked priority 1 of 4", "All required admission documents submitted by their deadline, and admission to the first-choice LiU programme in the First Notification of Selection Results (1 April 2027)", "Scholarship application during the short window that opens on results day - the page states no additional documents are needed to support it"]$$, $$https://liu.se/en/article/scholarships$$, NULL, NULL, $$not_published$$, NULL, NULL, $$[{"name": "LiU Scholarships 2027", "status": "first admission round: apply by 2027-01-15, documents/fee by 2027-02-01; First Notification of Selection Results (master) 2027-04-01; scholarship application opens early April 2027 for a short window - exact dates to be published on the LiU scholarships page (listed as TBD in LiU dates table)", "deadline_date": null}, {"name": "Annual pattern", "status": "scholarship application opens each year on the day students receive the Notification of Selection Results and is only open for a short window", "deadline_date": null}]$$, $$annual$$, $$Early April - on the day of the First Notification of Selection Results$$, $$Short window after opening; exact dates published yearly on the LiU scholarships page$$, $$upcoming$$, now(), now(), $$verified$$, 10, $$https://liu.se/en/article/scholarships$$, $$BATCH 27 NEW RECORD (2026-10-28): first LiU record in the catalogue. Evidence: official LiU scholarships page fetched first-hand (new source 3131) + LiU degree-studies dates (applications open 2026-10-16; deadline 2027-01-15; documents/fee 2027-02-01; master selection results 2027-04-01; 'LiU Scholarship application period: TBD'). Percentage encoded as variable (page: 'normally reduced by 50%', percentage/quantity set yearly; rules allow total or part coverage) - the aggregators' older 25/50/75 ladder is not used. min_gpa 3.5 encodes the page's official 4.0-scale anchor figure from the 2026 eligibility update; cross-scale equivalents stay textual. No fixed deadline exists yet for 2027 -> NULL/'not_published' + rounds. CATALOGUE GAP: universities has no Linköping row yet, so university_id is NULL and no university_scholarships row exists - create the university record + backlink in a later backlink batch (same backlog as 981 Karolinska / 986 IU Madinah).$$ , true, NULL, NULL, $$SEK$$, $$year$$, $$variable$$) RETURNING id, title;

-- 6) Source links (2533 is the pre-existing Axel Adler page source)
